{
  "schemaVersion": "2",
  "name": "Lab artifact view: Oby's runtime draws every board of a Claude Design canvas within its size",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "LAB-ARTVIEW-8 (src/lab/artifactview.rs: serve; core/assets/oby-dc/dc-runtime.js). Oby's own runtime of the .dc.html format, written from the format alone on React 18.3.1 vendored (no Babel, no CDN), draws the lab design's boards in chrome-headless-shell, each within its board's size and with no error: its holes filled from renderVals, a sibling board mounted by dc-import, a list from sc-for, a branch from sc-if, a link to another board played in place without the page leaving, #id scrolling, each board's data-props defaults given as its props (its tweaks, shown as they are). The canvas host shows every board of a page in its own sandboxed frame and switches pages. Then the Oby Artifacts canvas itself (its twelve boards, eight of them the interactive prototype, people's names replaced) publishes and every board draws with no error, each fixed-size one within its size, and its canvas host has every frame drawn.",
  "trigger": {
    "manual": {}
  },
  "tags": [
    "lab"
  ],
